  "title": "Irrationality of F(31/4) and the Exact Normalized Hankel Order",
  "subject": "Erdős #1049",
  "subject_kind": "problem",
  "form": "Problem note",
  "pages": 14,
  "question": "Which linear-form constructions fail at the rational base 3/2 for Erdős #1049, and what primitive kernel is still needed?",
  "precis": "For coprime integers a>b≥1, the paper proves irrationality of F(a/b) when log b / log a is below the explicit threshold (approximately 0.40568); in particular F((31/4)^r) is irrational for every positive integer r, with a uniform irrationality-exponent bound. This is an ordinary proof using Zudilin's polynomial conclusion; Lean checks finite subclaims rather than the irrationality theorem. A second construction proves the exact normalised Hankel order and leading coefficient. The criterion does not cover 3/2, where a primitive noncollapsed kernel and analytic remainder control are still needed.",
  "owns": "the problem-specific exposition for Erdős #1049: content and endpoint obstructions, the failed coordinatewise-clearing route, height arithmetic, and the remaining primitive construction",
